<title>USA: Sales of existing homes fell in August.</title>
<headline>Sales of existing homes fell in August.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sales of existing homes fell modestly in August, the National Association of Realtors said Wednesday, a third straight monthly decline as the housing market showed signs of leveling off.</p>
<p>The real estate lobby group said sales of existing, or used, homes fell 0.5 percent in August to a seasonally adjusted annual rate of 4.13 million. That followed a revised decline of 0.2 percent to 4.15 million in July and a sharper 2.8 percent drop in June sales.</p>
</text>
